Carafe Lab: an application gets the console's limit of 96 threads instead of 800.
On the console a process reaches threads=96/96 and the next svcCreateThread fails with LimitReached (0x10801);
Eden let it go on to 800, so a game that runs out of threads on the console kept running in Lab.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/core/hle/kernel/k_resource_limit.cpp
+++ b/src/core/hle/kernel/k_resource_limit.cpp
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@
 
     ASSERT(resource_limit->SetLimitValue(LimitableResource::PhysicalMemoryMax, physical_memory_size)
                .IsSuccess());
-    ASSERT(resource_limit->SetLimitValue(LimitableResource::ThreadCountMax, 800).IsSuccess());
+    ASSERT(resource_limit->SetLimitValue(LimitableResource::ThreadCountMax, 96).IsSuccess());
     ASSERT(resource_limit->SetLimitValue(LimitableResource::EventCountMax, 900).IsSuccess());
     ASSERT(
         resource_limit->SetLimitValue(LimitableResource::TransferMemoryCountMax, 200).IsSuccess());
